      "text": "To determine the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by \\(6\\), we first recognize that this is an arithmetic series.\n\nLet's denote the first term by \\(a_1\\) and the common difference \\(d\\):\n\\[\na_1 = 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad d = 7 - 1 = 6\n\\]\n\nUsing the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic series \\(a_n\\):\n\\[\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n\\]\n\nWe are given that the last term \\(a_n = 259\\). Therefore, we solve for \\(n\\):\n\\[\n259 = 1 + (n-1) \\times 6\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 1 from both sides:\n\\[\n258 = (n-1) \\times 6\n\\]\n\nDividing by 6:\n\\[\n43 = n-1 \\implies n = 44\n\\]\n\nNow we use the formula for the sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic series:\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a_1 + a_n)\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the known values:\n\\[\nS_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\times 260\n\\]\n\nCalculating the product:\n\\[\nS_{44} = 22 \\times 260 = 5720\n\\]\n\nTo find the remainder of \\(5720\\) when divided by \\(6\\), we determine the remainder of \\(5720\\) by \\(6\\):\n\\[\n5720 \\mod 6\n\\]\n\nWe perform the division:\n\\[\n5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2\n\\]\n\nSo, the remainder when \\(5720\\) is divided by \\(6\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
